Q:
Find the following limit using forms: lim as x -> infinity of (7^x-x)/x^7

A:
infinity

Dominant term in numerator: 7^x

Dominant term in denominator: x^7.

lim as x -> infinity of (7^x-x)/x^7 ~ lim as x -> infinity of 7^x/x^7

Form is infinity/infinity with much faster/slower -> infinity.

Thus lim as x -> infinity of 7^x/x^7 = infinity => lim as x -> infinity of (7^x-x)/x^7 = infinity

KEYWORDS: limits, infinity, dominant terms, exponential functions, polynomial functions
